A friend of mine recently acquired  an Alphastion 266XL. We were really
disappointed when we found out that this box is an ARC only machine. As we
did not like the idea of putting Windows NT on this machine, we decided to
install Alpha Linux on this box instead. Reading through the installation
guide we found out that the XL is essentially the same machine as an
Alphastation 400, which is SRM and Tru64 capable. Our sick minds ;) quickly
came up with a nice idea. Why not take out the flash chip, flash SRM on it
with a programmer and than put the chip back ?

After a bit digging at http://groups.google.com we found out that more
people where having a similar idea, but that nobody ever tried it.

I have a few questions:

Did anyone in this group every try this, and if so did it work ?

Where do I get an SRM image for the Alphastation 400 ? I downloaded the
official upgrade from Compaq, but it is a combined file. It contains a
bootloader, flash util and the SRM and ARC images. I tried to find out if it
would be easy to rip out the SRM image from this file. I searched the file
with the strings command to see if could find any strings I know from SRM.
As I did not find any, my guess is that it's either compressed or encrypted.
As we don't have an Alphastation 400, we also can't rip the image from the
chip.

Well if nobody ever tried this, and we can get a good SRM image, we are
probably going to try it, and see what happens :)

Any help is appreciated....

Desje




