Michael Joosten <joost@c-lab.de> writes:

> mips-tfile in a gcc compiled for Tru64/Alpha ???
> Verrry weird. Rather looks like your gcc has been the victim of a very
> confused installation...

Not at all.

> mips-tfile was needed for MIPS processors and their compiler/assembler
> tool chain, it merges debugging information into a specific ECOFF
> section of the object file.

Exactly, and mips-tfile is used on Tru64 UNIX for this specific reason: as
on some MIPS systems, the ECOFF object file format is used (the Alpha
toolchain is based on the MIPS one) and the native assembler provides no
way to get debug information into the object files.  The Compaq/HP
compilers are not affected by this problem but emit object code directly.

	Rainer

