Try df -k
I think you are probably more interested in filesystems than disks.
If you have ufs filesystems then df -k is enough to tell you all you
need, if you have advfs then you may need a little more work since
each advfs domain shares space with all of the filesets.
Try something like
cd /etc/fdmns
showfdmn *
That will probably tell you what you need to know although you
may need to filter it to make it look how you want.
Adam




