We had a problem just like this on a DEC-THREADS "C" program - turns out our
software people were not using reentrant system functions in the threads. I
happened upon the solution searching the net after I refused to grant the
software group an unlimited ULIMIT - I manage the Systems department.

Sounds like your FORTRAN program _somewhere_ is using a threads function.
The use of threads requires the use of the "reentrant" version of any system
functions involved in the thread - if you are using threads and
"non-reentrant" functions you will get unpredictable results and sporadic
crashes.

Take a close look at the DEC-THREADS documentation and try to find the
threads function being used.

Good luck,

Don Woodward


