Each file system treats the flags differently.  I only found evidence of 
autofs and ufs using the flags (and since mfs is based on ufs, I would 
expect it to use the ufs flags).  AdvFS most definitly does not use 
them.  It just stores them if a layered file system ask it to, and 
returns them (CFS, NFS, etc... layer on top of a physical file system, 
but I don't see either of them generating their own flags, so it looks 
like a mute point).  It does not appear that CFS, CDFS, DVDFS, NFS, ... 
uses the flags, but I did not have time for an exhaustive search.  I 
also do not know what they really mean since I'm not a ufs or autofs 
developer, nor to I care to learn :-)  Chances are the ufs meanings came 
from BSD, so I would suspect looking at one of the BSD distribution 
source code ufs implementations might show more information about some 
of these flags.

ufs (from /usr/include/ufs/inode.h)
    IRENAME          0x0004    /* inode is being renamed */
    IUPD             0x0010    /* file has been modified */
    IACC             0x0020    /* inode access time to be updated */
    ICHG             0x0040    /* inode has been changed */
    IMOD             0x0080    /* inode has been modified */
    ISHLOCK          0x0100    /* file has shared lock */
    IEXLOCK          0x0200    /* file has exclusive lock */
    ILWAIT           0x0400    /* someone waiting on file lock */
    INACTIVATING     0x0800    /* inode is being inactivated */
    INACTWAIT        0x1000    /* waiting for inode inactivation */
    IREADERROR       0x2000    /* disk read for inode failed */
    IQUOTA           0x4000    /* inode has quotas attached */
    IQUOTING         0x8000    /* quota attach in progress */
    IQUOTWAIT        0x10000   /* waiting while attach progresses */
    ICHGMETA         0x20000   /* Meta data changed and not on disk */
    IOLDDEVT         0x40000   /* TEMPORARY: this is an old devt */
    ICHGCTIME        0x80000   /* inode C-time is to be modified */
    IFSYNCING        0x1000000 /* fsync taking place on this inode. */
    IWAITFSYNC       0x2000000 /* Wait for inode's fsync to finish. */

ufs SysV environment (from /usr/include/s5fs/s5inode.h)
    S5IUPD           02        /* file has been modified */
    S5IACC           04        /* inode access time to be updated */
    S5IMOUNT         010       /* inode is mounted on */
    S5IWANT          020       /* some process waiting on lock */
    S5ITEXT          040       /* inode is pure text prototype */
    S5ICHG           0100      /* inode has been changed */
    S5ISYN           0200      /* do synchronous write for iupdate */
    S5IRENAME        0400      /* inode is being renamed */

autofs
    AUTOFS_INTERCEPT 0x10000000 /* intercept point */
    AUTOFS_OBJECT    0x20000000 /* in the AutoFS name space */

                                        Bob Harris


