For many years I worked in QC for a large firm.  One of the dilemmas
we faced was that some hardware problems refused to show up in
diagnostics, no matter how random the data.  Thus it was necessary to
run the actual platform operating systems and use the systems under
real-world loads to dig out problems that failed to show up otherwise.

Is that message appearing on the console?  The real "emergency-type"
problems sometimes do.

What does DECevent tell you?  Or EVM?  Even the old/obsolete uerf may
be picking up something relevant.  I'd bet there have been DECevent or
EVM events pertaining to this getting logged for some time.  You
should learn to use the standard error-reporting tools provided by the
vendor.

My guess, anyway, is that either the CPU and/or the L1 or L2 cache is
getting flaky.  Don't wait on this one.  Again this is just a guess,
but I believe you are a hair's breadth away from a totally-dead
system.

