Hi Ann,

As it turned out my simplistic trust in 5.0A was a little (only a little)
misplaced. I think I did everything correctly:

[1] Copy group and passwd into /var/yp/src.
[2] Use the sysman > Networks > NIS option to set NIS running in enhanced
mode. This created /var/yp/src/prpasswd.

However it would appear that by adding auth=local,yp into svc.conf I can now
set NIS account passwords using passwd. Certainly what didn't work before
now works. This entry wasn't made for me by sysman.

I'm using 5.0A because I was given a heap of DEC 3000 workstations which I
use for testing - I like these old boxes a lot, and was cursing like hell
when 5.1A told me my hardware was no longer supported :-(

